nd his cat are dancing.","alt":[],"t":"l","inferred":1},{"he":"מה האוכלוסייה של מצרים?","en":"What is the population of Egypt?","alt":[],"t":"l","inferred":1},{"he":"החתול שלנו לא שותֶה חלב.","en":"Our cat does not drink milk.","alt":[],"t":"t"},{"he":"החתולה שלי לומדת אנגלית.","en":"My female cat is learning English.","alt":[],"t":"l","inferred":1},{"he":"הסכין חותכת את האוכל שלנו.","en":"The knife cuts our food.","alt":[],"t":"t","inferred":1},{"he":"הילד שלה אוכל ארוחת צהריים.","en":"Her boy is eating lunch.","alt":[],"t":"l","audio":"https://d1vq87e9lcf771.cloudfront.net/he_v1/c1f67ef7c83c48ab60a9478af0c01770"},{"he":"הילדים שלהן אוכלים ארוחת בוקר.","en":"Their children are eating breakfast.","alt":["Their children eat breakfast."],"t":"t"},{"he":"אתה אוהב את ההרצאות של הפרופסור?","en":"Do you like the professor's lectures?","alt":[],"t":"l","inferred":1},{"he":"הילדים לוקחים את הכביסה מסבתא שלהם.","en":"The children take the laundry from their grandmother.","alt":[],"t":"l","inferred":1}],"hints":{"זה":"it / it is / it's","שלה":"her / her boys / her children","שלךָ":"your (sg.masc.) / yours (sg.masc.) / your (m.s)","שלי":"mine / my","הגמל":"the camel / the camel is","שלכם":"your / yours / yours(p.m.)","האוכל":"the food","שלךְ":"your (sg.masc.) / yours (sg.masc.) / your (m.s)","זאת":"it is (feminine) / that / that is (feminine)","אמא":"mom / mother / mum","שלו":"his / its","שייך":"belongs to (m.s)","לנו":"for us / to us / us","החתול":"the cat","של":"'s / Abraham's / avraham's","שרה":"f.s.","שלהן":"their (f)","התפוח":"the apple / the apple is","החלב":"milk / the milk / the milk is","הם":"are / they / they are","שייכים":"belongs to (m.p)","לכם":"do you have / to you (pl. masc.) / you","הסוס":"the horse / the horse is","שלך":"your (sg.masc.) / yours (sg.masc.) / your (m.s)","יפֶה":"beautiful / beautiful (sg. fem.) / handsome","לי":"I have / for me / me","כועסת":"f.s.","הוא":"(he) is / (it) is / he","שלנו":"our / ours","הילד":"the boy / the boy is / the kid","שמח":"happy (sg. masc.) / happy / happy (m.s)","אוכל":"eat / eating / eats","הכלב":"the dog","הולך":"walk, go (m.s - pres.) / walk, go / m.s.","שלהם":"their / theirs / their (m)","טעים":"delicious / tasty / tasty (m.s)","שלכן":"your (f.p)","מתוק":"sweet / sweet (m.s)","או":"or","הילדה":"the girl / the girl is","טעימה":"tasty (f.s)","אבא":"dad / father / father, dad","נהג":"driver","האם":"do / does / is","כן":"yes","אנחנו":"we / we are / we (c.p)","הילדים":"the boys / the children / the kids","לא":"aren't / didn't / do not","תחפושת":"a costume / costume","חיה":"animal","קורא":"is reading / read / reading","לךָ":"to you / you / do you have","אוכלים":"are eating / eat / eating","אוהבת":"like / likes / love","את":"it / that / the fruit","אברהם":"Abraham / Abraham's / avraham","אופָה":"bakes (m.s - pres.) / bakes (f.s - pres.)","עוגה":"a cake / cake","שייכת":"belongs to (f.s)","ספר":"a book / book / tell! (Story)","שותֶה":"drink / drinking / drinks","מים":"water","אתה":"you / you are / you (m.s)","מצטרף":"joins","היסטוריה":"history","מכירה":"f.s. / selling","יש":"I have / do you have / has","תשובה":"answer / answer, reply, solution","אני":"I / I am / I am a girl","אוהב":"like / likes / love","רוצֶה":"want / wants / would like","לאכול":"eat / eating / to eat","היא":"her / it / she","אוכלת":"are eating / eating / is eating","הגבר":"the man / the man is","רוקדים":"m.p.","מה":"everything / nothing can be done / there is nothing to do","מצרים":"Egypt","חלב":"milk","לומדת":"f.s.","אנגלית":"english","חותכת":"f.s.","ארוחת":"breakfast / lunch","צהריים":"lunch / noon","בוקר":"breakfast / breakfasts / for breakfast","לוקחים":"m.p."},"words":[{"he":"שלךָ","en":"your (sg.masc.)","alt":["yours (sg.masc.)"],"from":"lexicon","tr":"shel'kha"},{"he":"שלה","en":"her","alt":["her boys","her children","hers","its"],"from":"lexicon","tr":"shelah"},{"he":"אוהב","en":"love","alt":["like","likes"],"from":"lexicon","tr":"ohev"},{"he":"שלהם","en":"their","alt":["theirs"],"from":"lexicon","tr":"shelahem"},{"he":"שלכם","en":"yours","alt":["your","yours(p.m.)"],"from":"lexicon","tr":"shelakhem"},{"he":"הגמל","en":"the camel","alt":["the camel is"],"from":"lexicon"},{"he":"שלי","en":"my","alt":["mine"],"from":"skill","tr":"sheli"},{"he":"של","en":"'s","alt":["Abraham's","Avraham's","of","whose"],"from":"skill","tr":"shel"},{"he":"שלנו","en":"our","alt":["ours"],"from":"skill","tr":"shelanu"},{"he":"שלו","en":"his","alt":["its"],"from":"skill","tr":"shelo"},{"he":"שלכן","en":"Your (f.p)","alt":[],"from":"skill","tr":"shelakhen"},{"he":"שלהן","en":"Their (f)","alt":[],"from":"skill","tr":"shelahen"},{"he":"אברהם","en":"Abraham","alt":["Abraham's","Avraham","Avraham's"],"from":"skill"},{"he":"הילד","en":"the boy","alt":["the boy is","the kid"],"from":"phrase"},{"he":"אוכל","en":"eating","alt":["is eating","eats"],"from":"phrase","tr":"okhel"},{"he":"צהריים","en":"noon","alt":["lunch"],"from":"phrase","tr":"arukhat"},{"he":"זה","en":"this","alt":["this is","it is"],"from":"phrase","tr":"zeh"},{"he":"אני","en":"I","alt":["I am","me"],"from":"phrase","tr":"ani"},{"he":"את","en":"you","alt":[],"from":"phrase","tr":"at"},{"he":"האוכל","en":"the food","alt":[],"from":"phrase"}],"lexemes":["שלי","של","שלנו","שלךָ","שלהם","שלכם","שלו","שלה","שלךְ","שלכן","שלהן","לאברהם","אברהם"],"tips":"The word possessive word \"של\"\n--------------------------------\n\nIn Hebrew the basic possessive form is \"של\" (\"shel\" meaning \"of\"). של has additional forms for each person such as שלי (my), שלנו (our), like the other prepositions in Hebrew.\n\nTo say \"Yossi's apple\", we literally say \"The apple of Yossi\": התפוח של יוסי. \n\nNow let's have a look at the inflections of the word \"של\":\n\nEnglish | Hebrew\n---|---\nMy | של**י**\nYour (s.m.) | של**ךָ**\nYour (s.f.) | של**ךְ**\nHis | של**ו**\nHer | של**ה**\nOur | של**נו**\nYour (p.m.) | של**כם**\nYour (p.f.) | של**כן**\nTheir (m) | של**הם**\nTheir (f) | של**הן**\n\nWhen talking **about** a noun being possessed - we add the word \"ה\" (the) to the noun. When we are talking **to** the noun, no \"ה\" is needed.\n\nFor example: \n\n*Talking **about** the horse:*\n\n **ה**סוס שלי אוכל - My horse is eating. *Literally: \"the horse of mine is eating\" or \"the horse that is to me is eating\".*\n\n*Talking **to** the horse:*\n\n בוקר טוב, סוס שלי! - Good morning, my horse! *Literally: \"Good morning, horse of mine!\".*\n\nAs you will have noticed, in Hebrew the possessive word always comes **after** the noun and not before it.\n\nThat means we say: הסוס **שלי** and not **שלי** הסוס\n\nDo we always have to use the definite arcticle?\n-----------------------------\nThere is another case when we don’t need to use the word “ה” - certain nouns don’t require its use, even when we are talking about them. The most common example of such nouns is certain family members - for example, when talking about your:\n\nאבא - father/dad\n\nאמא - mother/mum/mom\n\nאח - brother\n\nאחות - sister\n\nFor example, אמא שלי חכמה - my mother is smart and not האמא שלי חכמה.\n\nThe phrase \"להיות שייך\"\n------------------\nIn Hebrew, like in English, you can use the word \"belong\" to indicate ownership. In Hebrew we use the word \"שייך\":\n\n-|Masculine|Feminine\n---|---|---\nSingular|שייך (shayákh)|שייכת (shayékhet)\nPlural|שייכים (shayakhím)|שייכות (shayachót)\n\nLike in English, this words requires the preposition \"to\" (\"-ל\" in Hebrew) which we learned in the \"There is\" skill.\n\nFor example:\n>\nזה שייך **לי**= It belongs to me\n>\nהחתולה שייכת **ל**ילד= the (female) cat belongs **to the** boy\n\nTechnically, שייך is (or was originally) an adjective, so it does not have an infinitive, or past and future tenses. The solution for this is to use the verb \"to be\" with שייך. \"To belong to\" is -להיות שייך ל."}